          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP715 - Bow River Valley&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Second cap on the north shore of the Bow Valley, on a late afternoon excursion inspired by van der Decken's logs published today.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684199440">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="51.103000" lon="-114.207183" />
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1074559">van der Decken</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP715 - Bow River Valley

Elev. 1112 metres&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since the past few days have been the first taste of spring that we've had this year, it would be churlish to complain about the stiff breeze coming out of the south. So I won't! I'll take warm and windy over calm and cold any day of the week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In spite of the beautiful conditions I didn't meet all that many people on the trails today. Maybe most folk had taken the chance to get out of the city? I don't know. I didn't even see all that many people working in their yards, which seemed odd as well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;People&lt;/em&gt; may have been failing to take advantage of the conditions, but I could see that the canine population wasn't neglecting their duties. Numerous conscientious dogs were down in the dog park at the bottom of the hill, making sure that their humans were been well exercised and entertained. I'm &lt;em&gt;sure&lt;/em&gt; that's how it works.... right? &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The marker post gave the game away as I rode up. And with the mania surrounding finding brass caps later, I knew this one would be well exposed. A quick wipe to remove a stray leaf and some grass was all that was needed to make the cap ready for its beauty shot. &quot;Beauty&quot; in this case is relative; that's one beat up old cap. Even blowing up the photographs failed to reveal a single digit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When I rode down to Inglewood on Thursday evening I hadn't seen even a single wildflower. Mother Nature made up for that oversight today. The south facing slopes here were covered in buffalo bean blooms. They're usually the first flowers I see after the crocuses, and they're finally out.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the excuse for a bike ride on a sunny day, and another brass cap, outforthehunt. (FOUND)&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
